# pyro_vortexconfinement

- Label: Pyro Vortex Confinement Force
- Category: Copernicus (`Cop`), Houdini 22.0.368
- Inputs: 0 to 4
- Parameters: 72 (exact, read from Houdini by hython)
- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/pyro_vortexconfinement.html
- Summary (EN): Pyro Vortex Confinement Force applies a vortex confinement force to a velocity field. It strengthens existing vortices to offset detail lost to diffusion during the fluid solver's diffusion stages. It outputs the modified velocities v.
- Résumé (FR) : Ce nœud renforce les tourbillons existants d'un champ de vitesse pour compenser la perte de détail due à la diffusion du solveur.

- Inputs meaning: ["v: Vector VDB containing the original velocities", "direction: Vector VDB for per-voxel control of the force direction", "threshold: Float or Vector VDB used as a threshold mask; a Vector VDB contributes its length", "control: Float or Vector VDB used as a control mask; a Vector VDB contributes its length", "angledir: Vector VDB for per-voxel control of the angle mask direction"]

- Key parameters: ["Activation: 1 turns the node on, 0 turns it off; the node has no effect unless set to 1", "Operation: Set (replace), Add, or Rotate (align with the incoming velocity direction)", "Type: First-order (fast and stable, more numerical diffusion) or second-order (better detail and energy preservation, slower and possibly unstable)", "Confinement Scale: strength of the confinement force", "Positive / Negative Diffusion Scale: positive smooths noise and spikes for stability; negative acts as anti-diffusion, concentrating energy toward vortex centres", "Kernel Size: size of the stencil used to compute curvature; larger gives smoother results", "Target Energy: smoothly clamps amplification above a set band energy to reduce instability", "Adaptive Confinement: limits confinement to areas where vortices are likely to form, reducing jitter", "Frequency Separation (Min/Max Swirl Size): restricts which swirl sizes are affected", "Threshold, Control, Angle and Axis masks: scale the effect by a range or direction, with optional ramps; Angle Mask uses Spread Angle (default 90 degrees), Axis Mask uses a world-space Axis Range"]

- Caveats: ["Requires DOP-level permissions. Not available in Houdini Core; works in FX, Apprentice, Indie and Education.", "The second-order method can introduce instabilities; the diffusion scale parameters are the suggested mitigation.", "Kernel Size and Frequency Separation both remove high-frequency detail, so aggressive values may remove useful detail.", "The node has no effect unless Activation is 1."]

